  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.2.1 — Bug fix.\n• Custom audio (AudioBytes) now plays even when the toast also has a BodyImage. Previously all audio was skipped for image toasts; a custom clip is an explicit opt-in and should always play. Named `Sound` cues and host mirroring are still skipped for image-only toasts (unchanged).\n\n0.2.0 — Additive, fully backward-compatible with 0.1.0.\n• Inline-markdown toast bodies: **bold**, *italic* / _italic_, `code`, ~~strikethrough~~. Parser is conservative — unpaired markers stay literal, so existing plain-text messages render unchanged.\n• Custom notification audio: ToastOptions.AudioBytes/AudioExt play an arbitrary clip via the new ToastAudio.PlayCustomBytes hook (Tostava stays dependency-free; the app supplies the player). The hook returns an IAudioPlayback so, when no explicit Duration is set, the toast lives exactly as long as the clip (progress bar = playback) and closing it with the X stops the sound. Named `Sound` cues are unchanged.\n• ToastOptions.BodyContent: render any Avalonia Control (a table Grid, a chart, …) full-width under the text. Tostava ships no table/chart engine — the consumer supplies the Control.",
